Core add-ons (very common)
---------------------------
1. CoreDNS
Service discovery inside cluster
Pod-to-pod DNS
Example:
payment.default.svc.cluster.local

2. kube-proxy
Handles Service networking
Routes traffic to pods


3. Amazon VPC CNI (aws-node)
Assigns VPC IPs to pods
Connects pod networking with AWS VPC
Storage add-ons

4. EBS CSI Driver
Attach Amazon Elastic Block Store volumes to pods

5. EFS CSI Driver
Mount Amazon Elastic File System shared storage
Ingress / Load balancing

6. AWS Load Balancer Controller
Creates ALB/NLB automatically

7. Ingress NGINX Controller
HTTP/HTTPS ingress routing
Monitoring


8. Metrics Server
CPU/memory metrics
Used by:
kubectl top pods
and HPA

9. Prometheus
Metrics collection

10. Grafana
Dashboards
Logging


11. Fluent Bit / Fluentd
Send logs to Amazon CloudWatch or Elasticsearch
Backup / DR

12. Velero
Backup and restore cluster resources
Security


13. Cert Manager
TLS certificates

14. External Secrets
Pull secrets from AWS Secrets Manager


15. OPA Gatekeeper / Kyverno
Policy enforcement
Autoscaling


16. Cluster Autoscaler
Adds/removes worker nodes

17. Karpenter
Dynamic node provisioning
GitOps / CD


18. Argo CD
GitOps deployments

19. Flux
GitOps
Service mesh


20. Istio
Traffic control
mTLS
observability

